  "provenance": "X1/P1 estimated stock housing union. Finite hotend CAD bands imported from community https://www.printables.com/model/533213 , Hotend.STEP (shared X1/P1 hotend geometry). Full stock housing/nozzle registration is NOT measured. Sources: https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/front-housing-assembly-p1p ; https://au.store.bambulab.com/products/front-housing-assembly-x1-series ; https://forum.bambulab.com/t/front-housing-assembly-x1-vs-p1s/67678 . Bambu specifies different housing connectors; community reports shell fit but different fan/LED wiring. That does not certify equal collision geometry. An estimated X1 lidar housing is included at X -35..-10, Y -35..15, Z 10..55 mm; the X1-series front housing source establishes the component, not these dimensions. P1S has no lidar: use bambu-p1s rather than this conservative family union. All assumed_* heater/sock/duct/fan/shroud/carriage bounds are author estimates, not dimensions obtained from these sources. Published gantry clearance: P1S inherits lower-rod height 34 mm and farther edge 33 mm from fdm_machine_common.json in BambuStudio https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio/tree/47a13eeb1d9af65ef2371e361c856e21d4f6ca72/resources/profiles/BBL/machine ; unknown near edge is over-approximated with symmetric Y span -33..33 mm, infinite X, top 100 mm. Door/enclosure and stationary auxiliary fan are machine-frame obstacles outside this moving head model, not nozzle-relative parts; this file assumes printing inside the nominal workspace and does not validate enclosure or out-of-workspace travel. Nozzle-tip frame: +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. 1 mm vertical/lateral margins do not certify the estimated body as safe. Tip allowance 3 mm/1 mm; external nozzle land radius 0.3 mm is from the CAD z=0 section, not the 0.4 mm bore. Only nozzle_land reaches z=0 (0..0.05 mm); next-section radii are confined to positive-Z finite bands. Body lower heights: sock 4, heater 5, ducts/shroud 5, fan 15, carriage 20, gantry 34 mm. Duct/shroud floor 5 mm replaces the unsupported 2 mm generic skirt assumption; it remains an unmeasured estimate, not a measured clearance increase. Not calibrated. Authored 2026-10-10.",
